    slug: 'administrative-assistant-wage-benchmark-2026', title: 'Administrative assistant wage benchmark: what the latest U.S. data can and cannot tell a small business',
    excerpt: 'Use the latest BLS wage figures as labor-market context, then separate the online work that may fit a Philippines-based assistant from duties that need local presence.', published: '2026-08-04', image: '/images/administrative-assistant-benchmarks-2026.png', imageAlt: 'Administrative assistant benchmark chart on a laptop',
    keyStats: [{value:'$47,460',label:'Median annual wage for secretaries and administrative assistants, May 2024',source:'BLS'}, {value:'$74,260',label:'Median for executive secretaries and executive administrative assistants',source:'BLS'}, {value:'35%',label:'Employed people who did some work at home on days worked in 2025',source:'BLS'}],
    takeaways: ['A U.S. wage median is a labor-market reference, not a quote for a remote staffing arrangement.', 'Executive, legal, medical, and general administrative work have different wage benchmarks.', 'The first hiring decision should be based on task location, access, review time, and approval rules.'],
    sections: [{heading:'Read the wage figure in context',body:'The Bureau of Labor Statistics reported a $47,460 median annual wage for secretaries and administrative assistants in May 2024. The lowest 10 percent earned less than $33,840 and the highest 10 percent earned more than $76,550. These are U.S. employee wage figures. They do not set the price, contract terms, or management cost of a Philippines-based remote arrangement.'},{heading:'The occupation label hides different work',body:'BLS reported a $74,260 median for executive secretaries and executive administrative assistants, $54,140 for legal secretaries and administrative assistants, $44,640 for medical secretaries and administrative assistants, and $46,290 for other secretaries and administrative assistants. A role brief should name the actual tasks and the judgment required instead of relying on the word assistant.'},{heading:'Turn the benchmark into a hiring brief',body:'Keep paper files, walk-in reception, local errands, and physical room preparation in a local lane. Online work such as inbox sorting, calendar preparation, CRM cleanup, research notes, and follow-up can fit a remote lane when the tools, examples, work hours, and stop rules are explicit. Review a small batch before expanding access.'}],
